https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/... (Steam no longer works after update to 51-RC1)
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/5296

Jonas Ådahl's tentative fix, posted on the bug report, for X11 windows
(Steam among them) becoming unclickable/inert after upgrading to
51-RC1. meta_window_x11_configure() stopped rebuilding the window's
shape and input regions when only its size changed (not its
stacking/visibility), so clicks landed on a stale input region that no
longer matched the window's actual client area. Track mutter!5296 for
the final upstream fix; this is the author's own workaround pending
review.

diff --git a/src/x11/window-x11.c b/src/x11/window-x11.c
index 5c2ac863b8..09a35a9d22 100644
--- a/src/x11/window-x11.c
+++ b/src/x11/window-x11.c
@@ -4722,5 +4722,9 @@ meta_window_x11_configure (MetaWindow *window)

   meta_window_notify_ready (window);
   if (!window->override_redirect)
-    meta_window_process_config (window, window_config);
+    {
+      meta_window_process_config (window, window_config);
+      meta_window_x11_update_shape_region (window);
+      meta_window_x11_update_input_region (window);
+    }
 }
